# Goal Tracking

## Before Starting Work

- Check GOALS.md for the current active goal.
- If no active goal exists for substantial work, create one with clear
  acceptance criteria before starting implementation.
- Confirm the goal status and acceptance criteria are current.

## During Work

- Keep changes scoped to the active goal.
- If work drifts from the goal, stop and reassess.
- Link tasks in CURRENT_TASKS.md to the active goal ID.
- Record research and decisions with goal references.

## Goal State Management

- Use status values: proposed, active, blocked, completed, canceled.
- Update the Goal Index table when any goal field changes.
- Fill the Verification table with commands, results, and evidence.

## Completion

A goal is not complete until:
- All acceptance criteria are met.
- Verification results are recorded in the goal's Verification table.
- WORKLOG.md has a completion checkpoint.
- CURRENT_TASKS.md reflects the completion.
- HANDOFF.md is updated if there are follow-up goals.

## Template

Copy from docs/templates/goal.md when adding new goals.
